==== Third-party: FFmpeg / 第三方组件：FFmpeg ====

ArcReel depends on the Python package imageio-ffmpeg (BSD-2-Clause), whose
platform wheels redistribute an unmodified, statically linked FFmpeg
executable. ArcReel runs that executable as a separate process for media
processing, and the Docker image ships it.

FFmpeg is Copyright (c) 2000-2024 the FFmpeg developers. The bundled builds are
configured with --enable-gpl and include GPL components such as libx264, so
they are licensed under the GNU General Public License. The Linux and Windows
builds are additionally configured with --enable-version3 (GPL version 3 or
later). The GPL version 3 text is in LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt.

Bundled builds (imageio-ffmpeg 0.6.0):
  - Linux x86_64 / aarch64: FFmpeg 7.0.2, static build by John Van Sickle
    (https://johnvansickle.com/ffmpeg/)
  - Windows x86_64: FFmpeg 7.1, build by gyan.dev
    (https://www.gyan.dev/ffmpeg/builds/)
  - macOS x86_64 / arm64: FFmpeg 7.1 static build
The binaries are published at
https://github.com/imageio/imageio-binaries/tree/master/ffmpeg

Corresponding source code:
  - FFmpeg release sources: https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ (ffmpeg-7.0.2 and
    ffmpeg-7.1), git tags n7.0.2 and n7.1 at https://git.ffmpeg.org/ffmpeg.git
  - The build configuration of each binary is printed by `ffmpeg -version`;
    the builders' pages above link the sources of the bundled libraries.

ArcReel 依赖 Python 包 imageio-ffmpeg（BSD-2-Clause），其平台 wheel 再分发未经修改的
静态链接 FFmpeg 可执行文件。ArcReel 以独立子进程调用它处理媒体，Docker 镜像亦随附
